{
  "rule": "nn_diffusion_duo",
  "metric": "Linf",
  "expected_min_order": 0.8,
  "notes": "dc/dv-weighted nearest-neighbor diffusion on a quasi-uniform triangular icosahedral mesh. The formula uses coeff = dc_edge / (dv_edge * area_eff) where area_eff = (1/4) * sum(dc * dv), the correct normalization area for the dc/dv FVM weight. Asymptotic L-inf convergence is first-order rather than second-order because cells adjacent to the Y11 zero-crossing at the geographic pole accumulate a constant ~7% relative error (the true Laplacian is O(h) there while the formula truncation error is of the same order), making the absolute L-inf error O(h). Over the level-2 (320 cells) -> level-3 (1280 cells) -> level-4 (5120 cells) sequence the observed orders are approximately [0.84, 0.96]; we require min order >= 0.8."
}